    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p class=\"TableTitle\"><strong>Table&nbsp;1.01</strong> Glossary of terms commonly used in the description of genetic tumour predisposition syndromes</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "Cree IA",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 97.0%; border-collapse: collapse; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" border=\"0\" width=\"97%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.38%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Term</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.62%; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-top-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"80%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Definition</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 1; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.38%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Allele</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.62%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"80%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Different versions of the same gene or variant</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 2; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.38%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Constitutional</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.62%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"80%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">A sequence variant present in all the body&rsquo;s cells, including the germ cells, that can therefore be passed on to offspring</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 3; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.38%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Gene</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.62%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"80%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">The basic unit of inheritance, containing the information encoding specific peptides/proteins or RNAs</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 4; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.38%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Germline</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.62%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"80%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">In this context, used similarly to &ldquo;constitutional&rdquo;, although usually regarded as defining the germ cells&nbsp;&ndash; the sperm and oocytes that pass on genetic material to offspring</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 5; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.38%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Mosaic(ism)</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.62%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"80%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">A genetic change present in some but not all cells in the body, caused by postzygotic mutation and resulting in multiple genotypes within the individual affected</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 6; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.38%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Penetrance</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.62%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"80%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">The proportion of individuals carrying a particular variant (or allele) of a gene (the genotype) that also expresses an associated trait (the phenotype)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 7; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.38%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Pathogenic</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.62%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"80%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">A genomic variant is called pathogenic if there is a direct link between the change and a particular condition or syndrome</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 8; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.38%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Postzygotic</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.62%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"80%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">A change in the genome that is acquired during the lifespan of an individual, instead of being inherited (see &ldquo;Mosaic(ism)&rdquo;)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 9; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.38%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Sequence</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.62%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"80%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">The sequence of nucleotide bases in DNA</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 10; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.38%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Somatic</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.62%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"80%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">The cells in the body other than sperm and oocytes (germ cells) and their gonadal progenitors</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 11; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.38%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Syndrome</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.62%; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"80%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">A set of medical signs and symptoms (and pathological abnormalities) which are correlated with each other and often associated with a particular disease or disorder</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 12; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.38%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Taxonomy</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.62%; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"80%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">An ordered arrangement of groups or categories, used to indicate relationships</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"mso-yfti-irow: 13; mso-yfti-lastrow: yes; page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 19.38%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Variant</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 80.62%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"80%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">A genetic variant is a permanent change in the DNA sequence</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  }
]